@startuml
!theme plain
title P1 Generic Media Ingest and Storage - Component View

actor "Pulsar App" as App
actor "Telegram Bot" as Tg
actor "Playback Node" as Node
actor "Authorized Control Actor" as Control

rectangle "Coordinator" {
  [Upload Session API] as UploadAPI
  [Telegram Media Adapter] as TgAdapter
  [SubmitMedia Service] as SubmitMedia
  [Quota + Idempotency Gate] as Gate
  [Signature Probe + ffprobe] as Probe
  [ffmpeg Normalizer] as Normalize
  [Media ACL + Delete API] as MediaAPI
  [Legacy Voice Mapper] as Legacy
  [Retention + Failed Upload Cleanup] as Retention
}

database "SQLite\nmedia_items/uploads/audit" as DB
folder "Storage\n(temp bytes + canonical WAV)" as Blob
collections "Transmission / Legacy Queue State" as Delivery

App --> UploadAPI : create session\nupload bytes
UploadAPI --> Gate
Gate --> SubmitMedia

Tg --> TgAdapter : voice/audio update
TgAdapter --> SubmitMedia : source=telegram

SubmitMedia --> Probe : magic bytes\nffprobe timeout
Probe --> Normalize : valid clip only
Normalize --> Blob : canonical WAV
Normalize --> DB : duration/hash/loudness/status
SubmitMedia --> DB : upload/media state\naudit metadata
SubmitMedia --> Legacy : compatibility WAV mapping
Legacy --> Delivery : after_current / play_voice bridge

Control --> MediaAPI : GET / DELETE media
Node --> MediaAPI : GET canonical media
MediaAPI --> DB : owner/target ACL\nrevocation/deleted state
MediaAPI --> Blob

Retention --> DB : expiry scan
Retention --> Blob : purge failed/temp/deleted bytes

note right of SubmitMedia
  Common entry point for app uploads and Telegram.
  No input becomes ready without probe, limits,
  canonicalization, and persisted status.
end note

note bottom of MediaAPI
  Phase 1 keeps legacy WAV compatibility while
  moving authorization and lifecycle into the
  generic media model.
end note

@enduml
